Tres upstream source tracking
============================

Tres 1.0.0 was released as a frozen upstream source tarball for the
project's first signed Ubuntu PPA uploads. GitHub's main branch has
since gained packaging and documentation updates and must not be
retrospectively tagged v1.0.0: it no longer represents that archive.

No upstream versioned Git tags or GitHub release assets have been
published yet. Therefore this initial Debian source package deliberately
has no debian/watch file. A watch rule scraping an empty GitHub tags
page reported "no matching files" during Debian Mentors QA.

When the next upstream source version is published, tag that actual
release revision (not the mutable main branch), add a version-5
debian/watch tracking GitHub tags or release assets, and test with
uscan --no-download --verbose.

The original 1.0.0 source archive should not be regenerated under the
same upstream version, as accepted distributions already retain it.
